.TH ARGON-CONTROL-CENTER 1 "November 2026" "argon-control-center 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
argon-control-center \- control center for Raspberry Pi computers in Argon40 cases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B argon-control-center
.RB [ \-\-gui | \-\-tui ]
.RB [ \-\-en | \-\-pt ]
.br
.B argon-control-center
.B \-\-status
|
.B \-\-json
|
.B \-\-doctor
.br
.B argon-control-center
.B \-\-stress
.I seconds
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B argon-control-center
monitors and configures a Raspberry Pi in an Argon40 case (Argon ONE, ONE V3, EON):
telemetry, GPU load, the
.B argononed
fan curve, board-aware overclocking with a trial boot and a stability test,
.I config.txt
hardware options, a GPIO lab and the
.B argononed
service.
.PP
Without options it opens the graphical interface. When there is no graphical
session (neither
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
nor
.B DISPLAY
is set) and standard output is a terminal, it opens the terminal interface
instead, for example over SSH.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Open the graphical interface even when no display is detected.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Open the terminal interface even inside a graphical session.
.TP
.BR \-\-pt ", " \-\-lang=pt
Use Brazilian Portuguese for the interface.
.TP
.BR \-\-en ", " \-\-lang=en
Use English for the interface.
.TP
.BR \-\-status ", " \-s
Print telemetry, the detected board and case, under-voltage events and the
current overclock, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a one-line JSON snapshot (CPU per core, clock, temperature, fan target,
memory, swap, disks, network, GPU load and CMA, firmware throttling flags,
5\ V alarm,
.B argononed
state, system information) and exit. Rates are computed against the previous
call, so the first call reports zero rates.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Report which hardware interfaces and tools the current user can use (I2C, GPIO,
firmware mailbox, GPU statistics, power sensor, trial boot, Polkit, I2C and GPIO
tools) and how to enable the missing ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-stress " seconds"
Load every CPU core for the given time while recording temperature, clock and
the 5\ V supply, then print a verdict. Exits with status 1 when the result is not
stable (throttling, temperature limit or under-voltage).
.SH TERMINAL INTERFACE
The terminal interface is read-only and refreshes every second. It shows the
.BR cpu ,
.BR mem ,
.BR net ,
.B gpu
and
.B argon
boxes with meters filled from left to right (0 to 100\ %) and a footer with the
board, system, kernel, uptime and load average.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit.
.TP
.BR ? ", " h
Show or hide the help window.
.PP
Use the graphical interface to change settings.
.SH DESKTOP WIDGETS
On KDE Plasma 6, the
.B Add Widgets
dialog lists the Argon widgets (CPU, Thermal, GPU, Memory, Network, Storage,
Power and System). They read
.B argon-control-center \-\-json
every two seconds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/argon-control-center/settings.json
Interface preferences.
.TP
.I /boot/firmware/config.txt
Firmware settings; the application manages a block between
.B # \-\-\- BEGIN ARGON CONTROL CENTER \-\-\-
and
.BR "# \-\-\- END ARGON CONTROL CENTER \-\-\-" .
The previous file is kept as
.IR config.txt.argoncc.bak .
.TP
.I /boot/firmware/tryboot.txt
Overclock under trial, used for a single boot.
.TP
.IR /etc/argononed.conf ", " /etc/argononed\-hdd.conf
Fan curves.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/argon-control-center/setup-permissions.sh
Creates the
.BR i2c " and " gpio
groups, installs the udev rules, loads
.B i2c\-dev
at boot and adds a user to the hardware groups.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when the terminal interface fails to start or
.B \-\-stress
finds an unstable system.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check what the current user can access:
.PP
.RS
.B argon-control-center \-\-doctor
.RE
.PP
Read the CPU temperature from a script:
.PP
.RS
.B argon-control-center \-\-json | jq .temp_c
.RE
.PP
Three-minute stability test:
.PP
.RS
.B argon-control-center \-\-stress 180
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vcgencmd (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR config.txt :
https://www.raspberrypi.com/documentation/computers/config_txt.html
.PP
Project page: https://github.com/wendelmax/argon-control-center
